msgid "What a value looks like, from its first character to its last. A character stands for itself. A class is one character out of several: <code dir=\"ltr\">[A-Z]</code>, <code dir=\"ltr\">[0-9a-f]</code>, <code dir=\"ltr\">[^ ]</code> for anything but a space, <code dir=\"ltr\">\\d</code> for a digit, <code dir=\"ltr\">\\w</code> for a letter, a digit or an underscore. A count follows what it counts: <code dir=\"ltr\">{4}</code>, <code dir=\"ltr\">{2,5}</code>, or <code dir=\"ltr\">?</code> for one or none. Alternatives are separated by <code dir=\"ltr\">|</code>, and a fixed separator sits in round brackets: <code dir=\"ltr\">( - )?</code>."
msgstr "Cén chuma atá ar luach, óna chéad charachtar go dtí an ceann deireanach. Seasann carachtar dó féin. Is éard is aicme ann ná carachtar amháin as roinnt: <code dir=\"ltr\">[A-Z]</code>, <code dir=\"ltr\">[0-9a-f]</code>, <code dir=\"ltr\">[^ ]</code> d’aon rud seachas spás, <code dir=\"ltr\">\\d</code> do dhigit, <code dir=\"ltr\">\\w</code> do litir, do dhigit nó d’fhostríoc. Leanann comhaireamh an rud a chomhaireann sé: <code dir=\"ltr\">{4}</code>, <code dir=\"ltr\">{2,5}</code>, nó <code dir=\"ltr\">?</code> do cheann amháin nó gan cheann. Scartar malairtí le <code dir=\"ltr\">|</code>, agus bíonn deighilteoir seasta idir lúibíní: <code dir=\"ltr\">( - )?</code>."

